# Scenario Changes Command

When the user asks for scenario-related tasks, follow the `scenario-changes` skill at `.cursor/skills/scenario-changes/SKILL.md`. The skill has three modes — detect which one to use from the trigger phrase.

## Trigger Phrases

### Branch Mode (default)

- "scenario changes"
- "generate scenario changes"
- "use-case changes"
- "what scenarios changed"
- "branch scenario summary"
- "PR summary"

### Full Project Mode

- "check whole project"
- "scan whole project"
- "full project scenarios"
- "scenario changes check whole project"
- "generate scenarios for whole project"

### Deep Page Scan Mode

- "deep scan {page}"
- "scan {page} deeply"
- "deep dive {page}"
- "analyze {page} sub-components"
- "drill into {page}"

## Mode Detection

- If the user's message contains "whole project", "full project", or "scan project" → use **Full Project Workflow** from the skill
- If the user's message contains "deep scan", "deep dive", "scan deeply", or "sub-components" with a page name → use **Deep Page Scan Workflow** from the skill
- Otherwise → use **Branch Workflow** from the skill

